    "summary": "Epic Dark Star > Other One marathon with soaring guitar and tight jam",
    "blurb": "The show delivers a monumental Dark Star into The Other One sequence followed by a high‑energy Turn On Your Lovelight and standout acoustic moments. Jerry’s tone soars while Phil locks in a lead‑style bass, and Pigpen adds organ flair on Katie Mae. The pristine soundboard capture makes this the definitive 2/13/70 Fillmore performance.",
    "review": "On February 13, 1970 at New York’s legendary Fillmore East, the Dead turned a late‑show slot into one of their most celebrated outings. An acoustic mini‑set segues into an electric onslaught highlighted by a marathon Dark Star that morphs seamlessly into The Other One, then bursts out into a fiery Turn On Your Lovelight and a blistering run through Smokestack Lightning. Jerry Garcia’s lead tone is in top form, soaring over Phil Lesh’s lock‑in, lead‑style bass lines, while Bob Weir provides solid rhythm and vocal power throughout. Pigpen’s organ and a rare guitar spot on Katie Mae add soulful texture, and the dual drumming of Mickey Hart and Bill Kreutzmann creates an other‑worldly pulse that propels the improvisations forward. The Miller soundboard source captures every nuance with crystal‑clear fidelity, making this recording the go‑to version for fans seeking both musical brilliance and pristine audio.",
